Image re-encoding (error level analysis and JPEG ghosts) uses the jpeg-encoder crate, whose IJG licence
requires this acknowledgement:
This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

The IJG standard quantization tables and their quality scaling (src/img/src/analysis/qt.rs) follow ITU-T T.81
Annex K and the Independent JPEG Group's libjpeg (jcparam.c).

Licences of all dependencies are checked against an allow-list (deny.toml; no GPL, AGPL or LGPL component).
